  "term": "intuitive knowledge",
  "definition": "Intuitive knowledge is knowledge gained by direct, immediate awareness rather than by reasoning through steps or using symbols. In this historical usage, it can mean sense-based or inner awareness, or knowledge in which the parts are directly present to the mind.",
